- `viewer.setShowLabels(true)` — Configures the `MultiViewer` widget so it will draw text labels (typically point indices/coordinates) next to the rendered geometry. It's a configuration call only; nothing is drawn yet.
- `viewer.show()` — A standard `QWidget` call that makes the viewer window actually appear on screen. Up to this point the widget is constructed in memory but invisible. The window will be filled in later as `simplify(...)` (line 932) reports results back through the `vptr` pointer.

Together they just enable text labels and pop up the window. The actual rendering happens during simplification via `vptr`, and the event loop that keeps the window responsive is started later by `app.exec()` at line 959 (after the `--out` file is written).

